user.admin
  Set up an admin account that logs in with an SSH key and uses sudo
  Applies to this host.
  Arms the safety timer.

Why
  Root and password logins are what attacks on SSH try first. A named account
  with a key and sudo is what lets ssh.server turn both off without locking you
  out.

Params (in the module's profile table)
  name (default "admin")
      Login name of the admin account.
  authorized_keys (default [])
      Public keys the account accepts; empty uses the keys of the user this
      session logged in as.
  sudo (default "nopasswd")
      "nopasswd" or "password" (the sudo group, for an account with a password).

Fixes these audit controls
  none
